All,

The certification body's lead assessor visits on 10 and 11 February for the yearly surveillance of our quality system certificate. A few reminders on how their findings work, because the rules are theirs and not ours.

They grade each finding as a major nonconformity, a minor nonconformity or an opportunity for improvement. A nonconformity of major severity means part of the system is missing or has broken down; for that, the auditee must send a corrective action plan within 30 days of the closing meeting, and the body may come back to verify it before the certificate continues. A minor nonconformity needs a plan within 90 days, checked at the next visit. An opportunity for improvement needs no answer at all, though we usually take them up.

Please do not argue the grade on the day. If you disagree, note it and tell me; we can raise it in writing with the body afterwards.

Have the last twelve months of internal review records, training files and the document register ready in the QA office. The assessor will choose sites to sample on the first morning.

Lunch for the assessor is arranged at the canteen; please do not take them out to a restaurant.

Neelam
